  "id": "huaiju_huai_opera",
  "name": "Huaiju (Huai opera)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Opera of northern Jiangsu sung in the Jianghuai dialect of Yancheng and Huai'an, which grew in the Qing dynasty from local xianghuo ritual drama and mentanci door-to-door songs and was carried to Shanghai by migrants from the region, where much of its twentieth-century development took place; it entered China's national intangible heritage list in 2008. Its arias rest on the huaidiao, ladiao and ziyoudiao tune families, led by a huqin fiddle (the erhu card stands in) with pipa, yangqin, drum and gong.",
  "recipe": "classic late-2000s huaiju, art Music, east Asian branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. bamboo stick horsehair threaded between strings erhu, pipa, yangqin, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, opera bending gong tamtam. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
